["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Coast deer live in thick cover and hunting barely dents them. You win by going slow, watching edges and staying out in the rain.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 325\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three ways to hunt black tailed deer. 1 still hunt the timber: slow, quiet, short shots, best on wet quiet days. 2 watch a cutblock edge at first and last light; cold sitting, keep layers. 3 partner walk to a stander, on foot only; agree zones of fire. Pick by weather and ground.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"325\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Three ways to hunt them</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"48\" width=\"372\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"72\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">1</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Still hunt the timber</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">+ Slow, quiet, short shots</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">Watch: Best on wet, quiet days</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"130\" width=\"372\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"154\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"159\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">2</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Watch a cutblock edge</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">+ First and last light</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">Watch: Cold sitting; keep layers</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"212\" width=\"372\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"236\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">3</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Partner walk to a stander</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">+ On foot only (99%)</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">Watch: Agree zones of fire</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Pick by weather and ground (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Three methods: still hunt, watch an edge, partner walk to a stander (Tip).</li><li>Pushes are on foot only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the methods, pros and cons</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Pros</th><th>Cons</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Still hunting\">Still hunting</button> the timber</td><td>You cover ground; close, quiet shots</td><td>Hard to do well; easy to bump deer (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Watch a <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Cutblock\">Cutblock</button> edge</td><td>You see deer before they see you; a rest for the shot</td><td>Cold, slow; only dawn and dusk (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Partner walk to a stander</td><td>Moves deer to a waiting hunter</td><td>Needs zones of fire and a plan (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>\"Hunting has little effect on black-tailed deer herds\" because coast forests hold so much security cover (90%, Nyberg and Janz 1990). Translation: deer have many places to hide (Tip).</li><li>Unlawful: \"to use a power boat, aircraft, or motor vehicle or other mechanical device to herd or harass wildlife\". Pushes are on foot only (99%, page 11, item 25).</li><li>Long glassing works less in timber than in open interior country (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Rule Book: Region 2</a> strategy).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A clearcut seen from above, ringed by forest cover. Deer use is concentrated in the band within 100 m of the cover. The centre of a big cut gets little use. Watch the edges, not the middle.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Cutblocks: the 100 m band</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"46\" width=\"372\" height=\"230\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"80\" width=\"280\" height=\"160\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#d9e4c8\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"110\" width=\"200\" height=\"100\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#f3f1e4\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">within 100 m of cover</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\">centre of a big cut:</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\">little use (90%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">forest (cover)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Most deer use is near the edge (90%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Watch the edges, not the middle (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Deer used clearcuts most within 100 m of cover <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>The middle of cuts over 400 m wide got very little use <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the cutblock numbers</summary><ul><li>Radio collared deer on Vancouver Island concentrated their use of clearcuts within 100 m of cover and used areas beyond 100 m less than expected (90%, Nyberg and Janz 1990, summarizing Kremsater 1989).</li><li>Openings under 200 m wide (under 100 m to cover from any point) give the most deer use, whatever their area <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Openings up to 400 m wide get less, but still real, use in the middle; centres of openings over 400 m wide get very little unless the ground gives some cover <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Use of cover next to clearcuts was highest within 200 m of the edge <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>What it means for you (Tip): sit where you can see the edge band, and expect most deer inside 100 m of the trees. Your shot will usually be under 150 m (Tip).</li><li>Cutblock ages and what grows: <a href=\"#/s/cutblock-country\">Cutblock country</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 322\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Still hunting in 4 steps. 1 wind in your face or across. 2 a few steps, then stop, and look longer than you walk. 3 look for parts: an ear, a leg, a flick. 4 rifle ready: shots are short in timber. All tips.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"322\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Still hunting in 4 steps</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"48\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"74\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">1</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Wind in your face</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">or across</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"110\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"136\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">2</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">A few steps, then stop</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">and look longer than you walk</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"172\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"198\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">3</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Look for parts</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">an ear, a leg, a flick</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"234\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"260\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">4</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Rifle ready</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"277\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">shots are short in timber</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">All Tips (hunter experience)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Look longer than you walk (Tip).</li><li>Look for parts, not a whole deer (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: still hunting detail (Tips)</summary><ul><li>Go into the wind or across it. Check it every few minutes with a puffer or thread (Tip).</li><li>A few steps, then stop and look. Move when cover hides you (Tip).</li><li>Look low and through the trees for a leg, an ear, the white of a throat, a tail flick (Tip). Good cover hides 90% of a deer at 60 m (85%, chapter 3).</li><li>Shots in timber are short and fast. Know your rifle off sticks and kneeling (Tip).</li><li>Full lesson: <a href=\"#/s/still-hunting\">Still hunting</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 322\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A rain day plan. 1 wet ground is quiet, good for still hunting. 2 rain can erase blood: shoot only good shots and track soon. 3 wool or synthetics, a rain shell and a spare dry layer. 4 shivering: stop, get dry, warm and fed, and head out.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"322\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Rain day plan</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"48\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"74\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">1</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Wet ground is quiet</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">good for still hunting</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"110\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"136\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">2</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Rain can erase blood</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">shoot only good shots; track soon</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"172\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"198\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">3</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Wool or synthetics</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">rain shell, spare dry layer</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"234\" width=\"372\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"260\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">4</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Shivering? Stop</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"277\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">get dry, warm, fed; head out</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">Tips, with the safety lessons</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rain is normal here. The coast forest zone is the rainiest in BC <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Wet ground is quiet underfoot (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: rain detail</summary><ul><li>The CWH (Coastal Western Hemlock) zone is the rainiest in BC: 1,000 to 4,400 mm a year, mean 2,228 mm (95%, <a href=\"#/s/wet-forest-country\">Wet forests</a>).</li><li>Rain softens leaves and covers noise, but you chill fast. Wool or synthetics, a rain shell, a spare dry layer (Tip).</li><li>Rain can erase a blood trail within about an hour (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/blood-trailing\">Blood trailing</a>). Take only a shot you are sure of; if rain is coming, track sooner (Tip). Chapter 6.</li><li>Shivering, clumsy hands, slurred words: early hypothermia. Stop, get dry and warm, eat, head for the truck (Tip; see <a href=\"#/s/cold-injuries\">Cold injuries</a>).</li><li>Deer behaviour in rain: no black tail study found. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> before trusting any \"they move in the rain\" rule.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 622\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Zones of fire, seen from above. Walking side by side: hunters A and B walk in sight of each other and in line. Each shoots only in an arc of about 45 degrees straight ahead of them; the wedge between them is NO SHOT. Small boat: two hunters sit back to back, the bow shooter covers the arc off the bow and the stern shooter the arc off the stern; never shoot toward your partner. Sit to shoot, never swing past your partner, motor off and anchored. The width of the boat arcs is an illustration only: no source gives an angle for a boat.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"622\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Walking side by side</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"236\" fill=\"#e9eddf\"/>\n<path d=\"M13 236 l2 -6 M17 236 l0 -7 M21 236 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#b9c29a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M390 159 l2 -6 M394 159 l0 -7 M398 159 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#b9c29a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g data-tip=\"Your zone of fire|The only slice of ground where you may shoot: about 45 degrees straight ahead. Every shot also needs a safe backstop. Sky is never one.\"><path d=\"M128 232 L63.7 76.8 A168 168 0 0 1 192.3 76.8z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g data-tip=\"Partner zone|B shoots only in their own slice. Never swing the muzzle outside your zone, even tracking a running deer.\"><path d=\"M272 232 L207.7 76.8 A168 168 0 0 1 336.3 76.8z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g data-tip=\"No shot zone|The middle and behind are no shot zones. A deer runs into the gap: hold fire.\"><path d=\"M128.0 232.0 L192.3 76.8 L207.7 76.8 L272.0 232.0z\" fill=\"#f6cfc0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO SHOT</text></g>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A shoots</text>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">here only</text>\n<text x=\"272\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B shoots</text>\n<text x=\"272\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">here only</text>\n<path d=\"M107.3 182.1 A54 54 0 0 1 148.7 182.1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">45°</text>\n<g data-tip=\"In sight, in line|Walk side by side, always in sight. Lose sight of each other: muzzles up or down, no shooting, call out.\"><line x1=\"144\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(128 232) rotate(0) scale(1.05)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(272 232) rotate(0) scale(1.05)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in sight, in line</text></g>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Each arc about 45 degrees, straight ahead</text>\n<line x1=\"14\" y1=\"318\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"318\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"346\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Small boat, back to back</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"358\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#dbe7ef\"/>\n<path d=\"M20 378 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M330 382 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M10 532 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M350 536 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M100 374 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M186 538 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g data-tip=\"Back to back|Two hunters sit back to back: the bow shooter faces forward, the stern shooter faces back. Shoot sitting, never stand. Arc width here is an illustration only: no source gives a boat angle.\"><path d=\"M168 446 L29.4 503.4 A150 150 0 0 1 29.4 388.6z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M236 446 L374.6 388.6 A150 150 0 0 1 374.6 503.4z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M112 424 H282 C312 424 334 438 344 446 C334 454 312 468 282 468 H112 C104 468 100 462 100 446 C100 430 104 424 112 424z\" fill=\"#c9b48a\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"106\" y=\"437\" width=\"10\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#55524c\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(168 446) rotate(270) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(236 446) rotate(90) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stern arc</text>\n<text x=\"354\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bow arc</text>\n<rect x=\"37.8\" y=\"508.0\" width=\"112.2\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"93.887\" y=\"527\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stern shooter</text>\n<line x1=\"164\" y1=\"456\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"508\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"456\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"252.0\" y=\"508.0\" width=\"105.8\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"304.903\" y=\"527\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bow shooter</text>\n<line x1=\"240\" y1=\"456\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"508\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"456\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<g data-tip=\"Never toward your partner|Never shoot toward your partner. Only one person moves at a time. Unload before anyone changes seats.\"><rect x=\"157.4\" y=\"362.0\" width=\"85.3\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO SHOT</text>\n<line x1=\"202\" y1=\"438\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"389\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"438\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#c92a2a\"/></g>\n<g data-tip=\"Loaded in a boat|From 1 October 2026, a BC hunting exemption allows a loaded firearm in a boat with no motor, or while the motor is not moving the boat.\"><text x=\"200\" y=\"570\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sit to shoot. Never swing past</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"591\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">your partner. Motor off, anchored.</text></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"614\" font-size=\"14\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#55524c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Boat arcs: illustration only, no sourced angle</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pair: one sits at the edge, the other walks slowly toward him, wind at the walker's back (Tip).</li><li>Agree zones of fire, a meeting point and a clock time (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pair and solo detail</summary><ul><li>Pair: the stander watches a cutblock edge or a trail crossing; the walker still hunts toward the stander so scent pushes deer ahead (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Your Harrison deer hunt</a>).</li><li>Orange: BC has no blaze orange law. Wear it anyway with a partner (95% for the law, Tip for the advice). Deer see orange as dull <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Solo: keep the pack out short, about 1 km or less and 100 m climb or less (Tip).</li><li>Leave a trip plan with someone at home: truck, road, time out (75%, AdventureSmart).</li><li>Full lesson: <a href=\"#/s/hunting-partner\">Hunting with a partner</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 332\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four shooting rules near Harrison. 1 never shoot on or across a road allowance. 2 within the 400 m bands along some Forest Service Roads, lawful hunting only, no target shooting. 3 no hunting or shooting within 100 m of a house, farm building or school. 4 Harrison Mills flats: no rifles, hunt the hills. Study aid only.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"332\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Where not to shoot near Harrison</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"46\" width=\"372\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"73\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">1</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Never on or across a road</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">road allowance: no shot (99%)</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"110\" width=\"372\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"137\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">2</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">400 m FSR bands</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">lawful hunting only, no target shooting</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"174\" width=\"372\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"201\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">3</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">100 m from buildings</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">house, farm building, school (99%)</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"238\" width=\"372\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"265\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">4</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Harrison Mills flats</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">no rifles: hunt the hills (99%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\">Study aid only. The regulations are the law.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Never shoot on or across a road allowance <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Some FSR (Forest Service Road) bands near Harrison ban shooting unless you are lawfully hunting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the Harrison road rules</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>No shooting on or across a road allowance (99%, page 10).</li><li>Unless lawfully hunting or trapping, no discharge within 400 m of the Francis Lake, Weaver Lake and Sts'ailes (West) FSRs and some FVRD (Fraser Valley Regional District) roads (99%, page 27). Hunting is allowed; target shooting is not (90%, my reading).</li><li>No hunting or shooting within 100 m of a house, farm building, school or regional district park (99%, pages 9 and 10).</li><li>Harrison Mills and the Nicomen lowland: no rifles (99%, Closed Areas Regulation; 85% my reading of the boundary). Hunt the hills.</li><li>All of it, with links: <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Your Harrison deer hunt</a>. The <a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a> shows the no shooting layer.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law): \"Slow is fast in the timber. If you think you are going slow, halve it.\"</p></aside>","<aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Walking logging roads all day and never stepping into the timber edge.</li><li>Sitting in the middle of a big cut instead of where you can see the edge.</li><li>Going home when it rains.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pick one cutblock edge for dawn. Sit 100 m back from the far edge with the wind in your face. Stay 2 hours.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Nyberg and Janz 1990, pages 37, 49 and 50 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Synopsis pages 9, 10, 11, 27 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Wet forests lesson <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Tactics: Tips. Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and link</summary><ul><li>Nyberg and Janz, editors (1990), <a href=\"https://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/pubs/docs/srs/Srs05.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Deer and Elk Habitats in Coastal Forests of Southern British Columbia\"</a>, pages 37, 49, 50, read directly from page images 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, 2 October 2026 edition, pages 9, 10, 11, 27, via <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Your Harrison deer hunt</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Biogeoclimatic data via <a href=\"#/s/wet-forest-country\">Wet forests</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>AdventureSmart trip plan advice via <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Your Harrison deer hunt</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Every tactic here is a Tip: hunter experience, not a study.</li></ul></details>"]